config FSLEK_FS
	tristate "fslek: mini RAM-based filesystem (CPE333)"
	help
	  A small RAM-based filesystem written for the CPE333 Operating
	  Systems mini-project. File contents live in a per-inode buffer
	  allocated with kvzalloc(); the directory tree lives in the dcache.
	  Everything is lost on unmount.

	  To compile this as a module, choose M here: the module will be
	  called fslek.

	  If unsure, say N.
